{"type":"message","id":"cb569f63","parentId":"bb11af2d","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:52:45.522Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking \"why what happened\" — they likely want an explanation of the feed-drain failure we just encountered. We need to explain:\n\n1. **Context**: A FEED_DRAIN cron triggered 16 minutes ago (12:36 UTC)\n2. **What it should have done**: Process stories from a feed card selection\n3. **What actually happened**: The feed_jobs database table was empty\n4. **Why**: The UUID `fe570e57-75de-49ac-980c-ecf7c4f551ab` doesn't correspond to any database row\n5. **Possible causes**: \n   - Stale/orphaned cron that fired after the feed card was already cleared\n   - Race condition where feed card creation didn't properly enqueue to feed_jobs\n   - Database cleanup/pruning removed the job before drain could run\n6. **Impact**: No stories processed, drain aborted early\n\nWe should also mention that we sent a status message to the Telegram group."},{"type":"text","text":"**🔍 Nexus — FEED_DRAIN Postmortem**\n\n**Timeline:**\n- `12:36 UTC` — FEED_DRAIN cron triggered: `fe570e57-75de-49ac-980c-ecf7c4f551ab`\n- `12:36 UTC` — Pipeline started, project: **coinography**\n- `12:36 UTC` — Database check revealed `feed_jobs` table empty\n- `12:37 UTC` — Aborted drain, sent status to Telegram group\n\n**Root Cause:**\nThe `feed_jobs` database table was **empty** for feed job ID `fe570e57-75de-49ac-980c-ecf7c4f551ab`. This UUID didn't correspond to any database row in `editorial.db`.\n\n**Why This Happens:**\n1. **Stale Cron Trigger** — The cron may have fired after the feed card was already cleared/expired\n2. **Race Condition** — Feed card creation (`send_feed_card.py`) may not have properly enqueued stories to `feed_jobs`\n3. **Database Cleanup** — Someone/something may have cleared `feed_jobs` manually\n4. **Orphaned Job** — Feed job was created but never persisted or was deleted before drain\n\n**Pipeline Steps Attempted:**\n1. ✅ Project detected: `coinography`\n2. ✅ Run initialized: `20260728-123745-33959-18206`\n3. ❌ Database check failed: `feed_jobs` empty\n4. ✅ Status message sent to Telegram group `-1003760909509`\n\n**Technical Detail:**\nThe pipeline expects `feed_jobs` table to contain rows where:\n- `feed_id` = UUID (from cron/feed card)\n- `selection_file` points to a JSON with story URLs\n- These get consumed by `build_picker_input.py --feed-job-id <INTEGER_ID>`\n\nBut here, the cron passed the UUID directly, while the script needs the **numeric integer `id`** column.\n\n**Impact:** No stories processed — safe abort.\n\n**Recommendation:**\n- Verify `send_feed_card.py` → `feed_jobs` enqueue logic\n- Check if feed cards expire or get cleaned up prematurely\n- Consider adding cron validation to skip drain if `feed_jobs` empty"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"deepseek.v3.2","usage":{"input":31432,"output":718,"cacheRead":256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32406,"cost":{"input":0.02011648,"output":0.00137138,"cacheRead":0.00004096,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.021528819999999997}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1785243143093,"responseId":"chatcmpl-7c11e8bb-eaa1-423f-8c54-1ccef11dcf44"}}
